    "text": "bowl (Pilot test). Full surface selects seed 22, while the unavailable hidden-MAE oracle selects seed 33. Gain versus the pool mean is -0.0888. The gallery exposes every case, including all losses. The full rule selects seed 22, whose generated upper bowl interior is visibly darker than the source. It has the lowest global color-histogram loss, whereas seed 33 has the best mean boundary term and much lower held-out error. The local rule chooses seed 33. Seed 22 covers essentially all held-out target pixels, so this particular error is not explained by missing-mask coverage alone. The example shows why matching a global distribution can conflict with the appearance of a particular part."
